import IUT.Applications.VojtaNumberField
import IUT.PaperIV.LegendreFrey

/-!
# Compactly bounded subsets of the line minus three points

Source: Mochizuki, *Arithmetic Elliptic Curves in General Position* ([GenEll]), the beginning of
§1 (page 3: `X^arc` and the complex conjugation `ι_X`), Definition 1.2
and Example 1.3 (pages 5 and 6), Definition 1.5 (page 8), Theorem 2.1 and its proof (pages 11 to
13), with its list of corrections, *Comments on "Arithmetic Elliptic Curves in General
Position"* (July 2016, pages 1 and 2: items (2), (5), (8), (9), (12)). Second source: Mochizuki,
*Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory IV*, Theorem A (page 3), the notation before Corollary 2.2
(page 40), Corollary 2.2 (pages 41 to 43: the statement with the condition `(*_{j-inv})`, parts
(i) to (iii), and the first paragraphs of the proof), Corollary 2.3 with its proof (pages 54 and
55) and Remark 2.3.1 (pages 55 and 56).
Pages read for this file: [GenEll] pages 3, 5, 6, 8 and 11 to 13; the corrections, pages 1 and 2;
IUT IV pages 3, 40 to 43 and 54 to 56. Pages checked against rendered images: all of these.

**What this file is.** It defines, on Mathlib objects, the compactly bounded subsets `K_V` of
`U(ℚ̄)` for `U = ℙ¹ \ {0, 1, ∞}`, states [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for this `U`
(`genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement Sig`, an open family) and the form to which the proof of IUT IV,
Corollary 2.3 reduces the corollary (`iutIVCor2_3ReducedFormStatement`, open), and proves how
these relate to `IUT.VojtaNumberField.VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree` and to the abc
conjecture `Challenge.ABC`. None of the open statements is proved, and nothing here bears on
whether the proofs in the papers are correct.

**Compactly bounded subsets (pages 5 and 6, corrections (8) and (9), Remark 2.3.1 (vi)).** A
compactly bounded subset is given by a finite set `V` of places of `ℚ` containing the
archimedean place and, for `v ∈ V`, a bounding domain `𝒦_v`: at `v = ∞` a nonempty
conjugation-stable compact domain (compact, equal to the closure of its interior) of
`X(ℂ)`; at a prime `v = p` a nonempty `Gal(ℚ̄_p / ℚ_p)`-stable subset of `X(ℚ̄_p)` whose
intersection with `X(K)` is a compact domain in `X(K)` for every finite extension `K ⊆ ℚ̄_p` of
`ℚ_p`. By correction (8) each `𝒦_v` lies in `U`. A point `x ∈ X(F)` lies in `K_V` when for every
`v ∈ V` the `[F : ℚ]` points of `X(ℂ)`, respectively `X(ℚ̄_p)`, determined by `x` lie in `𝒦_v`.
Formalization choices:
* `ℚ̄_p` is Mathlib's `PadicAlgCl p` with its spectral norm, `Gal(ℚ̄_p / ℚ_p)` is
  `PadicAlgCl p ≃ₐ[ℚ_[p]] PadicAlgCl p`, the finite extensions `K` are the finite dimensional
  `IntermediateField ℚ_[p] (PadicAlgCl p)` with the subspace topology; the points determined by
  `x ∈ F` are the images of `x` under the ring homomorphisms `F → ℂ`, respectively
  `F → PadicAlgCl p`.
* Since every `𝒦_v` avoids `∞` and the affine line is open in `ℙ¹`, the conditions are stated
  in the affine coordinate (`ℂ`, `E`); this loses nothing.
* `V` is recorded as the finite set `cbSupport` of its primes; the archimedean place is always
  in `V`. The data `cbPadic p` at primes outside `V` is carried but never used.
* The condition `𝒦_v ≠ X^arc`, respectively `𝒦_v ≠ X(ℚ̄_v)`, of page 6 is implied by `𝒦_v ⊆ U`.
* What is lost: the statement on page 6 that `V` and the `𝒦_v` are determined by the subset
  itself is not proved; here a compactly bounded subset is its data, and inclusion of point sets
  is `CbSubsetLE`.

**[GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (page 11).** It fixes a finite set `Σ` of primes and asserts that (i)
and (ii) are equivalent. Statement (i) concerns every hyperbolic curve over a number field; it is
not stated here, since curves, canonical sheaves and their heights are not defined in the
library. Its instance `X = P`, `D = C` is `VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree`; no new
definition is made for it. Statement (ii) is `genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement Sig`, with the point
representation of `IUT.VojtaNumberField` (a number field `F : Type` generated by
`x ∈ F \ {0, 1}`, `[F : ℚ] ≤ d`) and its functions `heightNF`, `logDiffNF`, `logCondNF`. The
constant depends on `d`, `ε` and `K_V`. Page 11 quantifies `d`, `ε`, `K_V` in this order; here
`K_V` comes before `ε` (adjacent universal quantifiers, so the meaning is the same), which lets
the piece for fixed `K_V` and `d` be named `cbDegreeAtMostStatement`.

**What (ii) ⟹ (i) needs (pages 11 to 13), not proved or assumed here.** Given `X`, `D`, `d`,
`ε`: a connected finite étale Galois covering `U_Y → U_X` ramified with index `e` over `D`
(page 11), with `d' = d deg(Y / X)` (page 12); Proposition 1.7 (i), (ii) and Proposition 1.4
(i), (ii), (iii) to reduce to `D = ∅` on `U_Y(ℚ̄)^{≤ d'}`; then, assuming the bound fails on
`X(ℚ̄)^{= d}`, compactness of `X(K)` over finite extensions `K` of `ℚ_v` for `v ∈ V` (with `V`
containing `∞` and `Σ`) to extract `Ξ` whose conjugates converge to `d`-tuples `Ξ_v`; the
noncritical Belyi map `φ : X → P` of [Mzk1] Theorem 2.5, unramified over `U_P` and sending the
points of `Ξ_v` into `U_P(ℚ̄_v)` (page 12); a compactly bounded `K_V ⊆ U_P(ℚ̄)` built from
neighborhoods of `φ(Ξ_v)` with `φ(Ξ) ⊆ K_V`; statement (ii) on `K_V` at the degree of `φ(Ξ)`;
Propositions 1.6, 1.7 (i) and 1.4 (i), (iii), and correction (5) to the last display (page 13).
On our reading (not a sentence of the paper), the passage uses (ii) at points of degree larger
than `d` even for `X = P`, `d = 1`.

**IUT IV Corollary 2.3 (pages 54 and 55).** Its proof says that the corollary coincides with
[GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (i), so by the equivalence it suffices to prove (ii) with support containing
`2`, and one may assume that `K_V` satisfies `(*_{j-inv})` of Corollary 2.2 (page 41): the image
of `𝒦_2` under the `j`-invariant `U_X → (ℳ_ell)_ℚ → 𝔸¹` lies in `2^{N} 𝒪_{ℚ̄_2}` for an integer
`N`. This form is `iutIVCor2_3ReducedFormStatement`, with the `j`-invariant of the Legendre
curve `y² = x(x - 1)(x - λ)` of page 41 (`IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreJ`, Mathlib's
`WeierstrassCurve.j` of that curve by `IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreCurve_jInv`; the formula is
computed in that module, not printed in IUT IV), and `𝒪_{ℚ̄_2}` the elements of norm at most `1`.
Page 55 says `(*_{j-inv})` is "entirely vacuous" for fixed `d`; the passage from the reduced form
back to (ii) for `Σ = {2}` is not proved here. Corollary 2.2 itself is not stated: the functions
`log(𝔮^∀)`, `log(𝔮^{⊢2})`, `ht_∞`, the exceptional sets `𝔈𝔵𝔠_d`, `𝔈𝔵𝔠_{ε,d}`, the invariant
`ε_E`, the fields `F_mod`, `F_tpd` and the initial Θ-data of Theorem 1.10 have no definition in
the library.

**Main results.**
* `genEllTheorem2_1ii_of_boundedDegree`, `cbDegreeAtMost_of_degreeAtMost`: (i) for `(P, C)`
  implies (ii), by restriction.
* `cbDegreeAtMost_mono_set`, `cbSubsetLE_of_domains`, `cbDegreeAtMost_mono_degree`,
  `genEllTheorem2_1ii_mono`: monotonicity in `K_V`, in `d` and in `Σ`.
* `iutIVCor2_3ReducedForm_of_genEll`: (ii) for `Σ = {2}` implies the reduced form.
* `cbDegreeOne_of_ABC`: the abc conjecture implies the degree one statement on every `K_V`
  (through `degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC`).
* `exists_ratio_bound`, `abc_on_arch_of_cbDegreeOne`: on `K_V` with `V = {∞}` the degree one
  statement gives the abc inequality exactly for the triples `a + b = c` with `a / c ∈ 𝒦_∞`, and
  these satisfy `δ c ≤ a`, `δ c ≤ b` for some `δ > 0` depending on `𝒦_∞`.
* `cbDegreeOne_iff_abcRatioBounded`: `cbDegreeOneAllStatement`, the degree one statement on all
  compactly bounded subsets, is equivalent to `abcRatioBoundedStatement` (abc for triples with
  `δ c ≤ a`, `δ c ≤ b`, every `δ > 0`); `abcRatioBounded_of_genEllEmpty`,
  `abcRatioBounded_of_ABC`. Whether `abcRatioBoundedStatement` implies `Challenge.ABC` is not
  addressed.
* Nonvacuity: `cbDiskQuarter` (support `{∞}`, the disk of radius `1/4` around `1/2`) contains
  infinitely many rational points (`cbDiskQuarter_rat_infinite`) and the point `1/3` of the
  triple `1 + 2 = 3` (`cbDiskQuarter_triple_one_two_three`).
* `isPadicBoundingDomain_two`, `cbTwoAdic`, `cbTwoAdic_nonvacuous`: a compactly bounded subset
  with support `{2, ∞}` satisfying `(*_{j-inv})` and containing the point `1/2` of `1 + 1 = 2`,
  so the reduced form of Corollary 2.3 and (ii) for `Σ = {2}` do not quantify over an empty
  class.

**Not proved.** (ii) ⟹ (i) of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (needs the Belyi map theorem of [Mzk1],
the étale covering, Propositions 1.4, 1.6, 1.7; none of them is formalized here); the vacuity of
`(*_{j-inv})` for fixed `d` (on our reading it needs finiteness of the set of extensions of `ℚ_2`
of bounded degree inside `ℚ̄_2`, which is not formalized here); that a compactly bounded subset
determines its support and bounding domains (page 6); any of the open statements.
-/

namespace IUT.CompactlyBounded

open NumberField
open IUT.VojtaNumberField IUT.ABCSpecialization

/-! ## Bounding domains and compactly bounded subsets -/

/-- A bounding domain at the archimedean place for `U = ℙ¹ \ {0, 1, ∞}` ([GenEll] Example 1.3
(ii), pages 5 and 6, with correction (8)): a nonempty compact subset `S` of `ℂ`, equal to the
closure of its interior, stable under complex conjugation (the involution `ι_X`), and contained
in `U(ℂ) = ℂ \ {0, 1}`. Compactness and the closure condition are taken in `ℂ`; since `ℂ` is open
in `ℙ¹(ℂ)` and `S` avoids `∞`, they agree with the conditions in `X^arc = ℙ¹(ℂ)`. -/
def IsArchBoundingDomain (S : Set ℂ) : Prop :=
  S.Nonempty ∧ IsCompact S ∧ closure (interior S) = S ∧ (∀ z ∈ S, starRingEnd ℂ z ∈ S) ∧
    (0 : ℂ) ∉ S ∧ (1 : ℂ) ∉ S

/-- A bounding domain at the prime `p` for `U = ℙ¹ \ {0, 1, ∞}` ([GenEll] Example 1.3 (ii),
pages 5 and 6, with correction (8)): a nonempty subset `S` of `U(ℚ̄_p) = ℚ̄_p \ {0, 1}`, with
`ℚ̄_p` Mathlib's `PadicAlgCl p`, stable under every `ℚ_p`-automorphism of `ℚ̄_p`, such that for
every finite extension `E` of `ℚ_p` inside `ℚ̄_p` the intersection `S ∩ E` is compact and equal to
the closure of its interior in `E` (subspace topology of the spectral norm). Since `E` is open in
`ℙ¹(E)` and `S` avoids `∞`, these are the conditions in `X(E) = ℙ¹(E)` printed on page 6. -/
def IsPadicBoundingDomain (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (S : Set (PadicAlgCl p)) : Prop :=
  S.Nonempty ∧ (∀ σ : PadicAlgCl p ≃ₐ[ℚ_[p]] PadicAlgCl p, ∀ z ∈ S, σ z ∈ S) ∧
    (0 : PadicAlgCl p) ∉ S ∧ (1 : PadicAlgCl p) ∉ S ∧
    ∀ E : IntermediateField ℚ_[p] (PadicAlgCl p), FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] E →
      IsCompact {z : E | (z : PadicAlgCl p) ∈ S} ∧
        closure (interior {z : E | (z : PadicAlgCl p) ∈ S}) = {z : E | (z : PadicAlgCl p) ∈ S}

/-- The data of a compactly bounded subset `K_V ⊆ U(ℚ̄)` of `U = ℙ¹ \ {0, 1, ∞}` ([GenEll]
Example 1.3 (ii), pages 5 and 6, with correction (8)): its support `V`, given by the finite set
`cbSupport` of the prime numbers in `V` together with the archimedean place, which `V` always
contains; a bounding domain `cbArch` at the archimedean place; and for each prime `p` of the
support a bounding domain `cbPadic p`. The value of `cbPadic p` for `p` outside the support plays
no role. The set itself is `cbMem`. -/
structure CompactlyBoundedSubset where
  /-- The primes of the support `V`; the archimedean place is always in `V`. -/
  cbSupport : Finset ℕ
  /-- The elements of `cbSupport` are prime numbers. -/
  cbSupport_prime : ∀ p ∈ cbSupport, p.Prime
  /-- The bounding domain at the archimedean place. -/
  cbArch : Set ℂ
  /-- It is a bounding domain. -/
  cbArch_domain : IsArchBoundingDomain cbArch
  /-- The bounding domains at the primes. -/
  cbPadic : ∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime], Set (PadicAlgCl p)
  /-- At each prime of the support, it is a bounding domain. -/
  cbPadic_domain : ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p ∈ cbSupport),
    haveI : Fact p.Prime := ⟨cbSupport_prime p hp⟩
    IsPadicBoundingDomain p (cbPadic p)

namespace CompactlyBoundedSubset

/-- The point `x` of a field `F` lies in the compactly bounded subset `K_V`: every embedding of
`F` into `ℂ` sends `x` into the archimedean bounding domain, and for every prime `p` of the
support every embedding of `F` into `ℚ̄_p` sends `x` into the bounding domain at `p`. For a
number field `F` these embeddings give the `[F : ℚ]` points of `X(ℂ)`, respectively `X(ℚ̄_p)`,
determined by `x` (page 6, with correction (9)). -/
def cbMem (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) (F : Type) [Field F] (x : F) : Prop :=
  (∀ σ : F →+* ℂ, σ x ∈ K.cbArch) ∧
    ∀ (p : ℕ) (hp : p ∈ K.cbSupport),
      haveI : Fact p.Prime := ⟨K.cbSupport_prime p hp⟩
      ∀ τ : F →+* PadicAlgCl p, τ x ∈ K.cbPadic p

/-- Inclusion of compactly bounded subsets, as sets of points over number fields. -/
def CbSubsetLE (K K' : CompactlyBoundedSubset) : Prop :=
  ∀ (F : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] (x : F), K.cbMem F x → K'.cbMem F x

end CompactlyBoundedSubset



/-! ## The statements -/

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: the inequality of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) on one
compactly bounded subset and one degree.** For every `ε > 0` there is a constant `C` such that
for every number field `F` generated by a point `x ∈ F \ {0, 1}` of `K_V` with `[F : ℚ] ≤ d`,
`ht(x) ≤ (1 + ε)(log-diff(x) + log-cond(x)) + C`. The constant depends on `K_V`, `d` and `ε`. -/
def cbDegreeAtMostStatement (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ (F : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] (x : F),
    IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {x} = ⊤ → Module.finrank ℚ F ≤ d → x ≠ 0 → x ≠ 1 →
      K.cbMem F x → heightNF F x ≤ (1 + ε) * (logDiffNF F + logCondNF F x) + C

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for the finite set `Sig` of
primes (the `Σ` of page 11).** For every positive integer `d`, every compactly bounded subset
`K_V ⊆ U_P(ℚ̄)` whose support contains `Sig` and every `ε > 0`, the inequality
`ht ≲ (1 + ε)(log-diff + log-cond)` holds on `K_V ∩ U_P(ℚ̄)^{≤ d}`. If `Sig` contains a number that
is not prime, no `K_V` qualifies and the statement holds trivially. -/
def genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement (Sig : Finset ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d → ∀ K : CompactlyBoundedSubset, Sig ⊆ K.cbSupport → cbDegreeAtMostStatement K d

/-- Condition `(*_{j-inv})` of IUT IV, Corollary 2.2 (page 41), for a compactly bounded subset
whose support contains `2`: the image of the bounding domain `𝒦_2 ⊆ U(ℚ̄_2)` under the
`j`-invariant of the Legendre curve `y² = x(x - 1)(x - λ)` lies in `2^N · 𝒪` for some integer
`N`, where `𝒪` is the ring of integers of `ℚ̄_2`, written as the elements of norm at most `1`.
The `j`-invariant is `IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreJ`, Mathlib's `WeierstrassCurve.j` of the
Legendre curve (`IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreCurve_jInv`). -/
def JInvBoundedAtTwo (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) : Prop :=
  ∃ N : ℤ, ∀ z ∈ K.cbPadic 2, ∃ o : PadicAlgCl 2, ‖o‖ ≤ 1 ∧
    IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreJ z = (2 : PadicAlgCl 2) ^ N * o

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: the form to which the proof of IUT IV, Corollary 2.3
(pages 54 and 55) reduces the corollary.** [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for `Σ = {2}`, asked only
for compactly bounded subsets that also satisfy `(*_{j-inv})`: for every positive integer `d`,
every compactly bounded `K_V` whose support contains `2` and which satisfies `(*_{j-inv})`, and
every `ε > 0`, `ht ≲ (1 + ε)(log-diff + log-cond)` on `K_V ∩ U(ℚ̄)^{≤ d}`. It is not Corollary
2.3, which concerns all hyperbolic curves and has no `K_V`. -/
def iutIVCor2_3ReducedFormStatement : Prop :=
  ∀ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d → ∀ K : CompactlyBoundedSubset, 2 ∈ K.cbSupport → JInvBoundedAtTwo K →
    cbDegreeAtMostStatement K d

/-- **An open statement, not a statement of the papers: the abc inequality for triples whose
ratios are bounded away from `0`.** For every `δ > 0` and `ε > 0` there is `C` such that every
triple of positive coprime `a`, `b` with `a + b = c`, `δ c ≤ a` and `δ c ≤ b` satisfies
`log c ≤ (1 + ε) log rad(abc) + C`. It is the degree one part of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for
`Σ = ∅` (`cbDegreeOne_iff_abcRatioBounded`). It is an auxiliary statement, not one of the
papers. -/
def abcRatioBoundedStatement : Prop :=
  ∀ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ → ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ a b c : ℕ, 0 < a → 0 < b → 0 < c →
    Nat.Coprime a b → a + b = c → δ * c ≤ a → δ * c ≤ b →
      Real.log c ≤ (1 + ε) * Real.log (Challenge.rad (a * b * c)) + C

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: the degree one statement on every compactly bounded
subset.** The degree one part of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for `Σ = ∅`. -/
def cbDegreeOneAllStatement : Prop :=
  ∀ K : CompactlyBoundedSubset, cbDegreeAtMostStatement K 1

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: the degree one statement on every compactly bounded
subset with support `{∞}`.** -/
def cbDegreeOneSupportFreeStatement : Prop :=
  ∀ K : CompactlyBoundedSubset, K.cbSupport = ∅ → cbDegreeAtMostStatement K 1

/-! ## Restriction and monotonicity -/

/-- **(i) ⟹ (ii) on one compactly bounded subset**: the statement for all points of degree at
most `d` restricts to the points of `K_V`, with the same constant. -/
theorem cbDegreeAtMost_of_degreeAtMost (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) {d : ℕ}
    (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost d) : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K d := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  exact ⟨C, fun F _ _ x hx hdeg h0 h1 _ => hC F x hx hdeg h0 h1⟩

/-- **The instance `(P, C)` of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (i) implies Theorem 2.1 (ii)** for every
`Sig` (page 11: "The fact that (i) ⟹ (ii) is immediate from the definitions"). -/
theorem genEllTheorem2_1ii_of_boundedDegree (Sig : Finset ℕ)
    (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree) : genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement Sig :=
  fun d hd K _ => cbDegreeAtMost_of_degreeAtMost K (h d hd)

/-- The statement on `K'` implies the statement on every smaller `K`, with the same constant. -/
theorem cbDegreeAtMost_mono_set {K K' : CompactlyBoundedSubset} {d : ℕ}
    (hKK' : CompactlyBoundedSubset.CbSubsetLE K K')
    (h : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K' d) : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K d := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  exact ⟨C, fun F _ _ x hx hdeg h0 h1 hK => hC F x hx hdeg h0 h1 (hKK' F x hK)⟩

/-- The statement in degree `d` implies the statement in every degree `d' ≤ d`. -/
theorem cbDegreeAtMost_mono_degree {K : CompactlyBoundedSubset} {d d' : ℕ} (hd : d' ≤ d)
    (h : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K d) : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K d' := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  exact ⟨C, fun F _ _ x hx hdeg => hC F x hx (hdeg.trans hd)⟩

/-- A larger set `Sig` of primes gives a weaker statement (fewer `K_V` qualify). -/
theorem genEllTheorem2_1ii_mono {Sig Sig' : Finset ℕ} (hS : Sig ⊆ Sig')
    (h : genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement Sig) : genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement Sig' :=
  fun d hd K hK => h d hd K (hS.trans hK)

/-- A sufficient condition for inclusion: a smaller support (as sets of conditions, the support
of `K'` is contained in that of `K`) and smaller bounding domains. -/
theorem cbSubsetLE_of_domains {K K' : CompactlyBoundedSubset}
    (hV : K'.cbSupport ⊆ K.cbSupport) (hA : K.cbArch ⊆ K'.cbArch)
    (hP : ∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime], p ∈ K'.cbSupport → K.cbPadic p ⊆ K'.cbPadic p) :
    CompactlyBoundedSubset.CbSubsetLE K K' := by
  intro F _ _ x ⟨hx, hxp⟩
  refine ⟨fun σ => hA (hx σ), fun p hp => ?_⟩
  have : Fact p.Prime := ⟨K'.cbSupport_prime p hp⟩
  exact fun τ => hP p hp (hxp p (hV hp) τ)

/-- **The reduced form of IUT IV, Corollary 2.3 follows from [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for
`Σ = {2}`** by dropping the condition `(*_{j-inv})`. -/
theorem iutIVCor2_3ReducedForm_of_genEll (h : genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement {2}) :
    iutIVCor2_3ReducedFormStatement :=
  fun d hd K h2 _ => h d hd K (Finset.singleton_subset_iff.mpr h2)

/-- **The abc conjecture implies the degree one statement on every compactly bounded subset**,
through `degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC`. No converse is claimed: a compactly bounded subset never
contains all of `U(ℚ)`, since its archimedean bounding domain is bounded and avoids
neighborhoods of `0` and `1`. -/
theorem cbDegreeOne_of_ABC (h : Challenge.ABC) (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) :
    cbDegreeAtMostStatement K 1 :=
  cbDegreeAtMost_of_degreeAtMost K (degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC.mpr h)

/-! ## Points of degree one -/

/-- A rational number generates `ℚ`. -/
theorem adjoin_rat_eq_top (q : ℚ) : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {q} = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.mpr fun z _ => by
    simpa using IntermediateField.algebraMap_mem (IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {q}) z

/-- The norm of a rational number in `ℂ` is its absolute value. -/
theorem norm_ratCast_complex (q : ℚ) : ‖(q : ℂ)‖ = |(q : ℝ)| := by
  rw [← Complex.ofReal_ratCast, Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_eq_abs]

/-- A point of a field `F` of degree one is a rational number, at which the three functions take
their rational values. -/
theorem degreeOne_values (F : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] (x : F)
    (hdeg : Module.finrank ℚ F ≤ 1) (h0 : x ≠ 0) (h1 : x ≠ 1) :
    ∃ q : ℚ, q ≠ 0 ∧ q ≠ 1 ∧ x = algebraMap ℚ F q ∧ heightNF F x = Height.logHeight₁ q ∧
      logDiffNF F = 0 ∧ logCondNF F x = Real.log (ratConductor q) := by
  have hF : Module.finrank ℚ F = 1 := le_antisymm hdeg Module.finrank_pos
  have hbij := Algebra.finrank_eq_one_iff_bijective_algebraMap.mp hF
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := hbij.2 x
  have hq0 : q ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; exact h0 (map_zero _)
  have hq1 : q ≠ 1 := by rintro rfl; exact h1 (map_one _)
  refine ⟨q, hq0, hq1, rfl, heightNF_algebraMap_rat F q, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [logDiffNF_eq, ← discr_eq_discr_of_ringEquiv (K := ℚ)
      (RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap ℚ F) hbij), Rat.numberField_discr]
    simp
  · rw [show algebraMap ℚ F q = RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap ℚ F) hbij q from rfl,
      logCondNF_ringEquiv, logCondNF_rat q hq0 hq1]

/-- For a compactly bounded subset with support `{∞}` (no primes), a rational number lies in it
exactly when it lies in the archimedean bounding domain. -/
theorem cbMem_rat_iff_of_support_eq_empty (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) (hV : K.cbSupport = ∅)
    (q : ℚ) : K.cbMem ℚ q ↔ (q : ℂ) ∈ K.cbArch := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    simpa [eq_ratCast] using h.1 (Rat.castHom ℂ)
  · intro h
    refine ⟨fun σ => by rwa [eq_ratCast], fun p hp => ?_⟩
    simp [hV] at hp

/-- A point of the archimedean bounding domain lies at distance at least `δ` from `0` and `1`,
for some `δ > 0` depending only on the domain, and at distance at most `R` from `0`. -/
theorem exists_arch_bounds {S : Set ℂ} (hS : IsArchBoundingDomain S) :
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧ ∃ R : ℝ, ∀ z ∈ S, δ ≤ ‖z‖ ∧ δ ≤ ‖z - 1‖ ∧ ‖z‖ ≤ R := by
  obtain ⟨hne, hc, -, -, h0, h1⟩ := hS
  obtain ⟨R, hR⟩ := isBounded_iff_forall_norm_le.mp hc.isBounded
  have hcont : ContinuousOn (fun z : ℂ => min ‖z‖ ‖z - 1‖) S :=
    (continuous_norm.min (continuous_norm.comp (continuous_id.sub continuous_const))).continuousOn
  obtain ⟨z0, hz0, hmin⟩ := hc.exists_isMinOn hne hcont
  have hz00 : z0 ≠ 0 := fun h => h0 (h ▸ hz0)
  have hz01 : z0 - 1 ≠ 0 := fun h => h1 (sub_eq_zero.mp h ▸ hz0)
  refine ⟨min ‖z0‖ ‖z0 - 1‖, lt_min (norm_pos_iff.mpr hz00) (norm_pos_iff.mpr hz01), R,
    fun z hz => ⟨(hmin hz).trans (min_le_left _ _), (hmin hz).trans (min_le_right _ _), hR z hz⟩⟩

/-- **The ratios of the triples whose point lies in an archimedean bounding domain are bounded
away from `0`.** There is `δ > 0` such that every triple of positive `a`, `b` with `a + b = c`
and `a / c ∈ 𝒦_∞` satisfies `δ c ≤ a` and `δ c ≤ b`. -/
theorem exists_ratio_bound (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) :
    ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧ ∀ a b c : ℕ, 0 < a → 0 < b → a + b = c →
      ((a : ℂ) / c) ∈ K.cbArch → δ * c ≤ a ∧ δ * c ≤ b := by
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, R, hR⟩ := exists_arch_bounds K.cbArch_domain
  refine ⟨δ, hδ, fun a b c ha hb habc hmem => ?_⟩
  have hc : (0 : ℝ) < c := by exact_mod_cast (show 0 < c by omega)
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, -⟩ := hR _ hmem
  have e1 : ((a : ℂ) / c) = (((a : ℝ) / c : ℝ) : ℂ) := by push_cast; ring
  have e2 : ((a : ℂ) / c) - 1 = ((-((b : ℝ) / c) : ℝ) : ℂ) := by
    have hc' : (c : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hc.ne'
    have hcab : (c : ℂ) = a + b := by exact_mod_cast habc.symm
    push_cast
    field_simp
    rw [hcab]; ring
  rw [e1, Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg (by positivity)] at h1
  rw [e2, Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_neg, abs_of_nonneg (by positivity)] at h2
  exact ⟨by rwa [le_div_iff₀ hc] at h1, by rwa [le_div_iff₀ hc] at h2⟩

/-- **The degree one statement on a compactly bounded subset with support `{∞}` gives the abc
inequality for the triples whose point `a / c` lies in its archimedean bounding domain.** By
`exists_ratio_bound` these triples have `δ c ≤ a` and `δ c ≤ b` for some `δ > 0`. -/
theorem abc_on_arch_of_cbDegreeOne (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) (hV : K.cbSupport = ∅)
    (h : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K 1) :
    ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ a b c : ℕ, 0 < a → 0 < b → 0 < c → Nat.Coprime a b →
      a + b = c → ((a : ℂ) / c) ∈ K.cbArch →
        Real.log c ≤ (1 + ε) * Real.log (Challenge.rad (a * b * c)) + C := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  refine ⟨C, fun a b c ha hb hc hab habc hmem => ?_⟩
  have hx0 : (a : ℚ) / c ≠ 0 :=
    div_ne_zero (by exact_mod_cast ha.ne') (by exact_mod_cast hc.ne')
  have hx1 : (a : ℚ) / c ≠ 1 := by
    rw [Ne, div_eq_one_iff_eq (by exact_mod_cast hc.ne')]
    exact_mod_cast (show a ≠ c by omega)
  have hm : K.cbMem ℚ ((a : ℚ) / c) := by
    rw [cbMem_rat_iff_of_support_eq_empty K hV]
    push_cast
    exact hmem
  have := hC ℚ _ (adjoin_rat_eq_top _) (Module.finrank_self ℚ).le hx0 hx1 hm
  rwa [heightNF_rat, logDiffNF_rat, logCondNF_rat _ hx0 hx1, zero_add,
    logHeight₁_of_triple ha hb hab habc, ratConductor_of_triple ha hb hab habc] at this

/-! ## Triples with ratios bounded away from `0` -/

/-- The norm of a rational number in `ℂ` in terms of its numerator and denominator. -/
theorem norm_ratCast_eq (q : ℚ) : ‖(q : ℂ)‖ = (q.num.natAbs : ℝ) / q.den := by
  rw [norm_ratCast_complex, Rat.cast_def, abs_div, Nat.cast_natAbs, Int.cast_abs,
    Nat.abs_cast]

/-- The distance from a rational number to `1` in `ℂ`, in terms of the numerator and the
denominator. -/
theorem norm_ratCast_sub_one_eq (q : ℚ) :
    ‖(q : ℂ) - 1‖ = ((q.num - q.den).natAbs : ℝ) / q.den := by
  have e : (q : ℂ) - 1 = -(((1 - q : ℚ)) : ℂ) := by push_cast; ring
  rw [e, norm_neg, norm_ratCast_eq, num_one_sub_eq_den_sub_num, den_one_sub_eq_den]
  congr 2
  omega

/-- **A rational point at bounded distance from `0`, `1` and `∞` gives a triple with ratios
bounded away from `0`.** If `δ ≤ |x|`, `δ ≤ |x - 1|` and `|x| ≤ R` (in the form
`δ den ≤ |num|`, `δ den ≤ |num - den|`, `|num| ≤ R den`), with `δ ≤ 1 ≤ R`, the triple of
`exists_triple_of_ne` satisfies `δ / (1 + R) · c ≤ a` and `δ / (1 + R) · c ≤ b`. -/
theorem exists_balanced_triple (x : ℚ) (h0 : x ≠ 0) (h1 : x ≠ 1) {δ R : ℝ}
    (hδ1 : δ ≤ 1) (hR : 1 ≤ R) (hN : δ * x.den ≤ x.num.natAbs)
    (hM : δ * x.den ≤ (x.num - x.den).natAbs) (hNR : (x.num.natAbs : ℝ) ≤ R * x.den) :
    ∃ a b c : ℕ, 0 < a ∧ 0 < b ∧ 0 < c ∧ a.Coprime b ∧ a + b = c ∧
      Height.logHeight₁ x ≤ Real.log c ∧ ratConductor x = Challenge.rad (a * b * c) ∧
      δ / (1 + R) * c ≤ a ∧ δ / (1 + R) * c ≤ b := by
  have hred : x.num.natAbs.Coprime x.den := x.reduced
  have hd : 0 < x.den := x.den_pos
  have hn0 : x.num ≠ 0 := Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr h0
  have hnd : x.num ≠ x.den := by
    intro h; apply h1
    rw [← Rat.num_div_den x, h, Int.cast_natCast, div_self (by exact_mod_cast hd.ne')]
  have hH : Height.logHeight₁ x = Real.log (max x.num.natAbs x.den : ℕ) :=
    Rat.logHeight₁_eq_log_max x
  have hcond : ratConductor x = ∏ p ∈ x.num.natAbs.primeFactors ∪
      (x.num - x.den).natAbs.primeFactors ∪ x.den.primeFactors, p := by
    unfold ratConductor; rw [num_sub_one_eq_num_sub_den]
  set N := x.num.natAbs with hN'
  set M := (x.num - x.den).natAbs with hM'
  set D := x.den with hD'
  have hlog : ∀ c : ℕ, max N D ≤ c → Height.logHeight₁ x ≤ Real.log c := fun c hc => by
    rw [hH]
    exact Real.log_le_log (by exact_mod_cast (show 0 < max N D by omega)) (by exact_mod_cast hc)
  have h1R : (0 : ℝ) < 1 + R := by linarith
  have key : ∀ a c : ℕ, δ * c ≤ (1 + R) * a → δ / (1 + R) * c ≤ a := fun a c h => by
    rw [div_mul_eq_mul_div, div_le_iff₀ h1R]; linarith
  have hN0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ N := Nat.cast_nonneg _
  have hM0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ M := Nat.cast_nonneg _
  have hD0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ D := Nat.cast_nonneg _
  have hδN : δ * N ≤ N := mul_le_of_le_one_left hN0 hδ1
  have hδM : δ * M ≤ M := mul_le_of_le_one_left hM0 hδ1
  have hδD : δ * D ≤ D := mul_le_of_le_one_left hD0 hδ1
  have hRN : (N : ℝ) ≤ R * N := le_mul_of_one_le_left hN0 hR
  have hRM : (M : ℝ) ≤ R * M := le_mul_of_one_le_left hM0 hR
  have hRD : (D : ℝ) ≤ R * D := le_mul_of_one_le_left hD0 hR
  rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hn0 with hneg | hpos
  · -- `x < 0`: `N + D = M`
    have hs : N + D = M := by omega
    have hsR : (M : ℝ) = N + D := by exact_mod_cast hs.symm
    refine ⟨N, D, M, by omega, hd, by omega, hred, hs, hlog M (by omega), ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [hcond, IUT.ABCSpecialization.rad_mul_mul_eq_prod_union (by omega) (by omega)
        (by omega)]
      congr 1; ext p; simp only [Finset.mem_union]; tauto
    · apply key; rw [hsR, mul_add]; linarith
    · apply key; rw [hsR, mul_add]; linarith
  rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hnd with hlt | hgt
  · -- `0 < x < 1`: `N + M = D`
    have hs : N + M = D := by omega
    refine ⟨N, M, D, by omega, by omega, hd, ?_, hs, hlog D (by omega), ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [← hs] at hred; exact Nat.coprime_self_add_right.mp hred
    · rw [hcond, IUT.ABCSpecialization.rad_mul_mul_eq_prod_union (by omega) (by omega)
        (by omega)]
    · apply key; nlinarith
    · apply key; nlinarith
  · -- `1 < x`: `M + D = N`
    have hs : M + D = N := by omega
    have hsR : (N : ℝ) = M + D := by exact_mod_cast hs.symm
    refine ⟨M, D, N, by omega, hd, by omega, ?_, hs, hlog N (by omega), ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [← hs] at hred; exact Nat.coprime_add_self_left.mp hred
    · rw [hcond, IUT.ABCSpecialization.rad_mul_mul_eq_prod_union (by omega) (by omega)
        (by omega)]
      congr 1; ext p; simp only [Finset.mem_union]; tauto
    · apply key; rw [hsR, mul_add]; linarith
    · apply key; linarith

/-- **The abc inequality for triples with ratios bounded away from `0` implies the degree one
statement on every compactly bounded subset.** A rational point of `K_V` lies in the
archimedean bounding domain, hence at distance at least `δ` from `0` and `1` and at most `R`
from `0`; `exists_balanced_triple` gives its triple, with ratios at least
`min δ 1 / (1 + max R 1)`. -/
theorem cbDegreeOne_of_abcRatioBounded (h : abcRatioBoundedStatement)
    (K : CompactlyBoundedSubset) : cbDegreeAtMostStatement K 1 := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, R, hR⟩ := exists_arch_bounds K.cbArch_domain
  have hδ₁ : 0 < min δ 1 := lt_min hδ one_pos
  have hR₁ : 1 ≤ max R 1 := le_max_right _ _
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h (min δ 1 / (1 + max R 1)) (by positivity) ε hε
  refine ⟨C, fun F _ _ x _ hdeg h0 h1 hmem => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨q, hq0, hq1, rfl, hH, hD, hCond⟩ := degreeOne_values F x hdeg h0 h1
  have hF : Module.finrank ℚ F = 1 := le_antisymm hdeg Module.finrank_pos
  have hbij := Algebra.finrank_eq_one_iff_bijective_algebraMap.mp hF
  let σ : F →+* ℂ :=
    (Rat.castHom ℂ).comp (RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap ℚ F) hbij).symm.toRingHom
  have hσ : σ (algebraMap ℚ F q) = (q : ℂ) := eq_ratCast (σ.comp (algebraMap ℚ F)) q
  have hz := hmem.1 σ
  rw [hσ] at hz
  obtain ⟨hz1, hz2, hz3⟩ := hR _ hz
  have hden : (0 : ℝ) < q.den := by exact_mod_cast q.den_pos
  rw [norm_ratCast_eq, le_div_iff₀ hden] at hz1
  rw [norm_ratCast_sub_one_eq, le_div_iff₀ hden] at hz2
  rw [norm_ratCast_eq, div_le_iff₀ hden] at hz3
  have hdq : (0 : ℝ) ≤ q.den := hden.le
  obtain ⟨a, b, c, ha, hb, hc, hab, habc, hle, hcond, hra, hrb⟩ :=
    exists_balanced_triple q hq0 hq1 (δ := min δ 1) (R := max R 1) (min_le_right _ _)
      hR₁ ((mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (min_le_left _ _) hdq).trans hz1)
      ((mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (min_le_left _ _) hdq).trans hz2)
      (hz3.trans (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (le_max_left _ _) hdq))
  rw [hH, hD, hCond, zero_add, hcond]
  exact hle.trans (hC a b c ha hb hc hab habc hra hrb)

/-! ## Disks around `1/2` and nonvacuity -/

/-- A rational number lies in the closed disk of radius `r` around `1/2` in `ℂ` exactly when
`|q - 1/2| ≤ r`. -/
theorem ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff (q : ℚ) (r : ℝ) :
    (q : ℂ) ∈ Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) r ↔ |(q : ℝ) - 1 / 2| ≤ r := by
  rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_eq_norm,
    show (q : ℂ) - 1 / 2 = (((q : ℝ) - 1 / 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) by push_cast; ring,
    Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_eq_abs]

/-- The closed disk of radius `r` around `1/2`, for `0 < r < 1/2`, is an archimedean bounding
domain. -/
theorem isArchBoundingDomain_closedBall {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 < r) (hr2 : r < 1 / 2) :
    IsArchBoundingDomain (Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) r) := by
  have hc : ((1 / 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) = (1 / 2 : ℂ) := by push_cast; ring
  refine ⟨⟨1 / 2, Metric.mem_closedBall_self hr.le⟩, isCompact_closedBall _ _, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [interior_closedBall _ hr.ne', closure_ball _ hr.ne']
  · intro z hz
    rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_eq_norm] at hz ⊢
    have e : starRingEnd ℂ z - 1 / 2 = starRingEnd ℂ (z - 1 / 2) := by
      rw [map_sub, ← hc, Complex.conj_ofReal]
    rw [e, Complex.norm_conj]
    exact hz
  · intro h
    have := (ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff 0 r).mp (by exact_mod_cast h)
    norm_num at this
    linarith
  · intro h
    have := (ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff 1 r).mp (by exact_mod_cast h)
    norm_num at this
    linarith

/-- The compactly bounded subset with support `{∞}` and archimedean bounding domain the closed
disk of radius `r` around `1/2`, for `0 < r < 1/2`. -/
noncomputable def cbDisk (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 < r) (hr2 : r < 1 / 2) : CompactlyBoundedSubset where
  cbSupport := ∅
  cbSupport_prime := fun p hp => by simp at hp
  cbArch := Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) r
  cbArch_domain := isArchBoundingDomain_closedBall hr hr2
  cbPadic := fun _ _ => ∅
  cbPadic_domain := fun p hp => by simp at hp

/-- **The degree one statement on every compactly bounded subset with support `{∞}` implies the
abc inequality for triples with ratios bounded away from `0`**: a triple with `δ c ≤ a` and
`δ c ≤ b` has its point `a / c` in the disk of radius `1/2 - min δ (1/4)` around `1/2`. -/
theorem abcRatioBounded_of_cbDegreeOne (h : cbDegreeOneSupportFreeStatement) :
    abcRatioBoundedStatement := by
  intro δ hδ ε hε
  have hδ₀ : 0 < min δ (1 / 4) := lt_min hδ (by norm_num)
  have hδ₀' : min δ (1 / 4) ≤ 1 / 4 := min_le_right _ _
  have hr : 0 < 1 / 2 - min δ (1 / 4) := by linarith
  have hr2 : 1 / 2 - min δ (1 / 4) < 1 / 2 := by linarith
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := abc_on_arch_of_cbDegreeOne (cbDisk _ hr hr2) rfl (h _ rfl) ε hε
  refine ⟨C, fun a b c ha hb hc hab habc hda hdb => hC a b c ha hb hc hab habc ?_⟩
  have hcR : (0 : ℝ) < c := by exact_mod_cast hc
  have hcab : (c : ℝ) = a + b := by exact_mod_cast habc.symm
  have h1 : min δ (1 / 4) * c ≤ a :=
    (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (min_le_left _ _) hcR.le).trans hda
  have h2 : min δ (1 / 4) * c ≤ b :=
    (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (min_le_left _ _) hcR.le).trans hdb
  have hx1 : min δ (1 / 4) ≤ (a : ℝ) / c := by rw [le_div_iff₀ hcR]; exact h1
  have hx2 : min δ (1 / 4) ≤ (b : ℝ) / c := by rw [le_div_iff₀ hcR]; exact h2
  have hsum : (a : ℝ) / c + b / c = 1 := by rw [← add_div, ← hcab, div_self hcR.ne']
  have e : ((a : ℂ) / c) = (((a : ℚ) / c : ℚ) : ℂ) := by push_cast; ring
  show ((a : ℂ) / c) ∈ Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) (1 / 2 - min δ (1 / 4))
  rw [e, ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff]
  push_cast
  rw [abs_le]
  constructor <;> linarith

/-- **The degree one part of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for `Σ = ∅` is equivalent to the abc
inequality for triples with ratios bounded away from `0`.** Neither side is proved here. -/
theorem cbDegreeOne_iff_abcRatioBounded :
    cbDegreeOneAllStatement ↔ abcRatioBoundedStatement :=
  ⟨fun h => abcRatioBounded_of_cbDegreeOne fun K _ => h K, cbDegreeOne_of_abcRatioBounded⟩

/-- [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) for `Σ = ∅` implies the abc inequality for triples with ratios
bounded away from `0`. -/
theorem abcRatioBounded_of_genEllEmpty (h : genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement ∅) :
    abcRatioBoundedStatement :=
  abcRatioBounded_of_cbDegreeOne fun K _ => h 1 le_rfl K (Finset.empty_subset _)

/-- The abc conjecture implies the abc inequality for triples with ratios bounded away from
`0`. -/
theorem abcRatioBounded_of_ABC (h : Challenge.ABC) : abcRatioBoundedStatement :=
  cbDegreeOne_iff_abcRatioBounded.mp fun K => cbDegreeOne_of_ABC h K

/-- The compactly bounded subset of support `{∞}` whose archimedean bounding domain is the
closed disk of radius `1/4` around `1/2`. -/
noncomputable def cbDiskQuarter : CompactlyBoundedSubset :=
  cbDisk (1 / 4) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)

/-- **`cbDiskQuarter` contains infinitely many rational points of `U`**: the numbers
`1/2 + 1/(4(n + 1))`. -/
theorem cbDiskQuarter_rat_infinite :
    {q : ℚ | cbDiskQuarter.cbMem ℚ q ∧ q ≠ 0 ∧ q ≠ 1}.Infinite := by
  refine Set.infinite_of_injective_forall_mem
    (f := fun n : ℕ => (1 / 2 : ℚ) + 1 / (4 * ((n : ℚ) + 1))) ?_ ?_
  · intro m n hmn
    have h := add_left_cancel hmn
    rw [one_div, one_div, inv_inj] at h
    have : (m : ℚ) = n := by linarith
    exact_mod_cast this
  · intro n
    have hpos : (0 : ℚ) < 1 / (4 * ((n : ℚ) + 1)) := by positivity
    have hle : 1 / (4 * ((n : ℚ) + 1)) ≤ 1 / 4 := by
      rw [div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) (by norm_num)]
      have : (0 : ℚ) ≤ n := Nat.cast_nonneg n
      linarith
    refine ⟨?_, by positivity, ?_⟩
    · rw [cbMem_rat_iff_of_support_eq_empty _ rfl]
      show _ ∈ Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) (1 / 4)
      rw [ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff]
      push_cast
      rw [add_sub_cancel_left, abs_of_pos (by positivity),
        div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) (by norm_num)]
      have : (0 : ℝ) ≤ n := Nat.cast_nonneg n
      linarith
    · intro h
      linarith

/-- **An abc triple in `cbDiskQuarter`.** The triple `1 + 2 = 3` gives the point `1/3`, which
lies in `cbDiskQuarter` (`|1/3 - 1/2| = 1/6 ≤ 1/4`), with height `log 3`, log-different `0` and
log-conductor `log 6 = log rad(1 · 2 · 3)`. -/
theorem cbDiskQuarter_triple_one_two_three :
    cbDiskQuarter.cbMem ℚ (1 / 3) ∧ heightNF ℚ (1 / 3) = Real.log 3 ∧ logDiffNF ℚ = 0 ∧
      logCondNF ℚ (1 / 3) = Real.log 6 := by
  have hH := logHeight₁_of_triple (a := 1) (b := 2) (c := 3) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide) rfl
  have hC := ratConductor_of_triple (a := 1) (b := 2) (c := 3) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide) rfl
  have hrad : Challenge.rad (1 * 2 * 3) = 6 := by
    rw [show (1 * 2 * 3 : ℕ) = 2 ^ 1 * 3 ^ 1 by norm_num,
      IUT.ABC.rad_mul_of_coprime (by decide), IUT.ABC.rad_prime_pow Nat.prime_two (by decide),
      IUT.ABC.rad_prime_pow Nat.prime_three (by decide)]
  simp only [Nat.cast_one, Nat.cast_ofNat] at hH hC
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, logDiffNF_rat, ?_⟩
  · rw [cbMem_rat_iff_of_support_eq_empty _ rfl]
    show _ ∈ Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) (1 / 4)
    rw [ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff]
    push_cast
    rw [abs_le]
    constructor <;> norm_num
  · rw [heightNF_rat, hH]
  · rw [logCondNF_rat _ (by norm_num) (by norm_num), hC, hrad]
    norm_num

/-! ## A compactly bounded subset whose support contains `2` -/

/-- The norm of `2` in `ℚ̄_2` is `1/2`. -/
theorem norm_two_padicAlgCl : ‖(2 : PadicAlgCl 2)‖ = 1 / 2 := by
  have h := PadicAlgCl.norm_extends 2 (2 : ℚ_[2])
  rw [map_ofNat] at h
  rw [h]
  have := Padic.norm_p (p := 2)
  push_cast at this
  rw [this]; norm_num

/-- The norm of `1/2` in `ℚ̄_2` is `2`. -/
theorem norm_half_padicAlgCl : ‖(1 / 2 : PadicAlgCl 2)‖ = 2 := by
  rw [norm_div, norm_one, norm_two_padicAlgCl]; norm_num

/-- A point of the closed ball of radius `1` around `1/2` in `ℚ̄_2` has `|z| = |z - 1| = 2`. -/
theorem norm_eq_two_of_mem_ball_half {z : PadicAlgCl 2} (hz : ‖z - 1 / 2‖ ≤ 1) :
    ‖z‖ = 2 ∧ ‖z - 1‖ = 2 := by
  have e1 : z = (z - 1 / 2) + 1 / 2 := by ring
  have e2 : z - 1 = (z - 1 / 2) + (-(1 / 2)) := by ring
  constructor
  · rw [e1, IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_eq_max_of_norm_ne_norm
      (by rw [norm_half_padicAlgCl]; linarith),
      norm_half_padicAlgCl]
    exact max_eq_right (by linarith)
  · rw [e2, IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_eq_max_of_norm_ne_norm
      (by rw [norm_neg, norm_half_padicAlgCl]; linarith),
      norm_neg, norm_half_padicAlgCl]
    exact max_eq_right (by linarith)

/-- **The closed ball of radius `1` around `1/2` in `ℚ̄_2` is a bounding domain at `2`**: it
avoids `0` and `1`, is stable under `Gal(ℚ̄_2 / ℚ_2)` (the spectral norm is invariant,
`spectralNorm_eq_of_equiv`), and meets every finite extension `E` of `ℚ_2` in a closed ball of
`E`, which is compact (`FiniteDimensional.proper`) and open and closed (ultrametric). -/
theorem isPadicBoundingDomain_two :
    IsPadicBoundingDomain 2 {z : PadicAlgCl 2 | ‖z - 1 / 2‖ ≤ 1} := by
  refine ⟨⟨1 / 2, by simp⟩, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro σ z hz
    simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hz ⊢
    have : σ z - 1 / 2 = σ (z - 1 / 2) := by
      rw [map_sub, map_div₀, map_one, map_ofNat]
    rw [this, ← PadicAlgCl.spectralNorm_eq, ← spectralNorm_eq_of_equiv σ,
      PadicAlgCl.spectralNorm_eq]
    exact hz
  · simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, zero_sub, norm_neg, norm_half_padicAlgCl]; norm_num
  · simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
    rw [show (1 : PadicAlgCl 2) - 1 / 2 = 1 / 2 by ring, norm_half_padicAlgCl]; norm_num
  · intro E hE
    have hS : {z : E | ((z : PadicAlgCl 2)) ∈ {z : PadicAlgCl 2 | ‖z - 1 / 2‖ ≤ 1}} =
        Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : E) 1 := by
      ext z
      simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_eq_norm]
      rfl
    have hP : ProperSpace E := FiniteDimensional.proper ℚ_[2] E
    rw [hS]
    refine ⟨isCompact_closedBall _ _, ?_⟩
    rw [(IsUltrametricDist.isOpen_closedBall (1 / 2 : E) one_ne_zero).interior_eq,
      Metric.isClosed_closedBall.closure_eq]

/-- On that ball the `j`-invariant of the Legendre curve has norm at most `1`: the numerator
`2⁸(z² - z + 1)³` has norm at most `2⁻⁸ · 4³` and the denominator `z²(z - 1)²` has norm `16`. -/
theorem norm_legendreJ_le_one_of_mem {z : PadicAlgCl 2} (hz : ‖z - 1 / 2‖ ≤ 1) :
    ‖IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreJ z‖ ≤ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := norm_eq_two_of_mem_ball_half hz
  have hq : ‖z ^ 2 - z + 1‖ ≤ 4 := by
    have a := IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max (z ^ 2 - z) 1
    have b := IsUltrametricDist.norm_add_le_max (z ^ 2) (-z)
    rw [← sub_eq_add_neg, norm_neg, norm_pow, h1] at b
    rw [norm_one] at a
    have : ‖z ^ 2 - z‖ ≤ 4 := b.trans (by norm_num [h1])
    exact a.trans (max_le this (by norm_num))
  unfold IUT.LegendreFrey.legendreJ
  rw [norm_div, norm_mul, norm_mul, norm_pow, norm_pow, norm_pow, norm_pow, h1, h2,
    norm_two_padicAlgCl]
  rw [div_le_one (by norm_num)]
  have : ‖z ^ 2 - z + 1‖ ^ 3 ≤ 4 ^ 3 := pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) hq 3
  nlinarith

/-- A compactly bounded subset with support `{2, ∞}`: the disk of radius `1/4` around `1/2` at
`∞`, and the ball `|z - 1/2| ≤ 1` of `ℚ̄_2` at `2`. -/
noncomputable def cbTwoAdic : CompactlyBoundedSubset where
  cbSupport := {2}
  cbSupport_prime := fun p hp => by simp at hp; subst hp; exact Nat.prime_two
  cbArch := Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) (1 / 4)
  cbArch_domain := isArchBoundingDomain_closedBall (by norm_num) (by norm_num)
  cbPadic := fun p _ => {z : PadicAlgCl p | ‖z - 1 / 2‖ ≤ 1}
  cbPadic_domain := fun p hp => by simp at hp; subst hp; exact isPadicBoundingDomain_two

/-- **The reduced form of Corollary 2.3 quantifies over a nonempty class**: `cbTwoAdic` has `2` in
its support, satisfies `(*_{j-inv})` (with `N = 0`), and contains the point `1/2` of the triple
`1 + 1 = 2`. -/
theorem cbTwoAdic_nonvacuous :
    2 ∈ cbTwoAdic.cbSupport ∧ JInvBoundedAtTwo cbTwoAdic ∧ cbTwoAdic.cbMem ℚ (1 / 2) := by
  refine ⟨Finset.mem_singleton_self 2, ⟨0, fun z hz => ⟨_, norm_legendreJ_le_one_of_mem hz,
    by rw [zpow_zero, one_mul]⟩⟩, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro σ
    rw [eq_ratCast]
    show _ ∈ Metric.closedBall (1 / 2 : ℂ) (1 / 4)
    rw [ratCast_mem_closedBall_iff]
    norm_num
  · intro p hp
    simp only [cbTwoAdic, Finset.mem_singleton] at hp
    subst hp
    intro τ
    show ‖τ (1 / 2) - 1 / 2‖ ≤ 1
    rw [eq_ratCast]
    push_cast
    simp

end IUT.CompactlyBounded
